    "title": "Count Nice Pairs in an Array",
    "category": "Hashing",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "problemStatement": "For an integer x, define rev(x) as the integer obtained by reversing its decimal digits. Count the number of index pairs (i, j) such that i < j and nums[i] + rev(nums[j]) = nums[j] + rev(nums[i]).",
    "input": "\u2022 First line contains integer N. \u2022 Second line contains N integers.",
    "output": "Print the number of nice pairs.",
    "constraints": "\u2022 1 \u2264 N \u2264 2\u00d710^5"
